{"id":"NCT06739122","title":"A Study of Dulaglutide (LY2189265) 3.0 mg and 4.5 mg in Pediatric Participants With Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus (AWARD-PEDS PLUS)","official":"A Phase 3, Open-Label, Multicenter, Single-Arm Study to Evaluate Safety, Tolerability, Pharmacokinetics, and Efficacy of Dulaglutide 3.0 mg and 4.5 mg in Pediatric Participants 10 to Less Than 18 Years of Age With Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus","summary":"The main purpose of this study is to evaluate additional dosing options for dulaglutide in pediatric participants with Type 2 Diabetes. Participation in this study will last about 8 months.","conditions":["Type 2 Diabetes"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Dulaglutide"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Have Type 2 diabetes treated with diet and exercise and metformin and/or basal insulin. Metformin and/or basal insulin dose must be stable for at least 8 weeks prior to screening.\n* Have a body weight ≥50 kilograms (kg) and Body Mass Index (BMI) of \\>85th percentile\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Have Type 1 diabetes\n* Have received treatment with any glucose-lowering agent(s) other than metformin, basal insulin, or dulaglutide within 8 weeks prior to screening\n* After the Type 2 diabetes diagnosis, have a history of diabetic ketoacidosis or hyperosmolar syndrome\n* Have had ≥1 episode of severe hypoglycemia and/or ≥1 episode of hypoglycemic unawareness within the last 6 months\n* Have family or personal history of medullary thyroid carcinoma (MTC) or multiple endocrine neoplasia syndrome type 2 (MEN2)\n* Have prior chronic, recurrent, or idiopathic pancreatitis, or known gallbladder disease\n* Have been treated with prescription drugs or over-the-counter medications that promote weight loss within 8 weeks prior to screening","minAge":"10 Years","maxAge":"17 Years","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":55,"start":"2025-01-10","pcd":"2027-12","upd":"2026-08-07","sponsor":"Eli Lilly and Company","areas":["other"],"central":["Trial questions or participation questions: 1-877-CTLILLY (1-877-285-4559) or · 1-317-615-4559 · LillyTrials@Lilly.com","Physicians interested in becoming principal investigators please contact · clinical_inquiry_hub@lilly.com"],"sites":[{"f":"University of Arizona","city":"Tucson","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85724","s":"R","lat":32.2217,"lon":-110.9265,"c":"520-626-3197"},{"f":"Arkansas Childrens Hospital","city":"Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72202-3500","s":"R","lat":34.7465,"lon":-92.2896,"c":"505-272-5551"},{"f":"Division of Endocrinology, Diabetes, and Metabolism","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90027","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":""},{"f":"UCLA Mattel Children's Hospital","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90095","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"310-203-7631"},{"f":"University of California, San Francisco","city":"San Francisco","pr":"California","zip":"94158","s":"R","lat":37.7749,"lon":-122.4194,"c":"415-514-6234"},{"f":"Children's Hospital of Colorado","city":"Denver","pr":"Colorado","zip":"80045","s":"NYR","lat":39.7392,"lon":-104.9847,"c":"20-777-3618"},{"f":"Yale Diabetes Research","city":"New Haven","pr":"Connecticut","zip":"06511","s":"R","lat":41.3081,"lon":-72.9282,"c":"203-737-7177"},{"f":"Emerson Clinical Research Institute","city":"Washington D.C.","pr":"District of Columbia","zip":"20009","s":"R","lat":38.8951,"lon":-77.0364,"c":"202-239-0777"},{"f":"Children's National Medical Center","city":"Washington D.C.","pr":"District of Columbia","zip":"20010","s":"R","lat":38.8951,"lon":-77.0364,"c":"888-884-2327"},{"f":"Nemours Children's Health","city":"Jacksonville","pr":"Florida","zip":"32207","s":"R","lat":30.3322,"lon":-81.6556,"c":""},{"f":"D&H National Research Centers, Inc","city":"Miami","pr":"Florida","zip":"33155","s":"R","lat":25.7743,"lon":-80.1937,"c":"786-375-6210"},{"f":"AdventHealth Orlando","city":"Orlando","pr":"Florida","zip":"32803","s":"R","lat":28.5